Explanation: The paragraph heavily relies on the foundational Threshold Algorithm (TA) [25] and its extensions, including cost-based optimizations and early stopping strategies [8], which are central to understanding top-k retrieval methods. Probabilistic top-k methods [48] provide a key comparison for handling uncertain data. Index-based approaches such as the onion layer [10] and view-based techniques [18,29] offer important baselines for query acceleration through structural or materialized reuse. In distributed environments [39], algorithms aim to minimize communication while preserving correctness, which is crucial in understanding the paragraph's context. Continuous top-k monitoring [41] and comprehensive surveys [17, 31] are mentioned briefly but still contribute to the overall grounding of the paragraph.
